  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nAbove normal moisture will remain in the area most of the week with \nPWAT values near 2\". Our best chance for rain will be mid-week as a \nmid-level disturbance moving across the Gulf enters the region. \nOtherwise, low chances for showers and thunderstorms can be expected \neach afternoon with the aid of the seabreeze, with the best chances \nacross the Victoria Crossroads. The ample moisture and warm \ntemperatures this week will promote elevated hist risk conditions \neach day. Heat index values will be within 105-110 degrees each \nafternoon with a moderate to high risk of heat-related impacts. If \nworking outdoors, make sure to take frequent breaks and hydrate \nadequately. \n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
